{
  "id": 163829911,
  "iid": 7330,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "epan: Fix return value of proto_strlcpy when not enough room",
  "description": "proto_strlcpy in normal situations returns the number of bytes\ncopied (because the return value of g_strlcpy is strlen of the\nsource buffer). It can copy no more than dest_size - 1, because\ndest_size is the size of the buffer, including the null terminator.\n(https://docs.gtk.org/glib/func.strlcpy.html)\n\nReturning dest_size can cause offsets to get off by one and reach\nthe end of the buffer, and can cause subsequent calls to have\nbuffer overflows. (See #16905 for an example in the comments.)",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2022-07-03T13:26:03.353Z",
  "updated_at": "2022-07-05T22:29:05.879Z",
